-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",15,{
[449]="70066BE2\n1\tTalk to Meneldir and tell him about yourself\tMeneldir, who was once a Ranger, has asked you to tell him where you call home.\n",
[450]="700190F0\n1\tPost signs (quantity: see journal)\tPosts ideal for hanging confusing signs can be found inside the hedge maze on the Horse-fields of Bree. Gísi has invited you to partake in the Elf-mockery he has devised by having you hang signs pointing all different directions. This should make the Elves even more lost, if that is possible.\n2\tTalk to Gísi outside the maze in the Horse-fields\tGísi is outside the hedge maze, waiting for increased delight in the plight of the lost Elves. You should bring Gísi the news that his plan went well, and the Elves certainly seem no closer to finding a way out.\n",
[451]="70000202\n1\tComplete Articles of Cunning\030Complete Implements of the Night\tSterling Proudfoot knows of a legendary burglar who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tSpeak to Sterling Proudfoot\tSterling Proudfoot is in Buckland, west of Bree and east of the Brandywine River. Now that you have acquired your new weapon and armour you should speak to Sterling Proudfoot.\n3\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins\tThe whereabouts of Bilbo Baggins are unknown by Sterling Proudfoot. Sterling Proudfoot thinks you should find the legendary burglar, Bilbo Baggins, and see what you might learn from him.\n",
[452]="700012D7\n1\tComplete Implements of War\030Complete Articles of Command\tDawn Stockard knows of a legendary captain who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Dawn Stockard\tDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree, in Bree-land.\n3\tTalk to Boromir in Rivendell\tBoromir is currently staying at Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Dawn Stockard has learned that Boromir, a great captain of Gondor, has come north to Eriador and is staying with the Elves. She believes he may teach you some of his techniques if you speak with him before he begins his journey home.\n",
[453]="7006421E\n1\tComplete 'Implements of Navigation'\030Complete 'Articles of Ingenuity'\tAelindil at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel knows of a legendary mariner who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Aelindil in Tornhad\tAelindil is at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n3\tTalk to Galdor in Rivendell\tGaldor can be found near Elrond's Stables, in Rivendell. You have fashioned a weapon and piece of jewellery worthy of your skill and reputation as a Mariner. Aelindil has asked you to seek out the Elf, Galdor, in Rivendell, that he might train you in the finer techniques of the Mariner.\n",
[454]="70002D82\n1\tComplete Implements of Daring\030Complete Articles of Valour\tGwesgylliel knows of a legendary champion who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Gwesgylliel at Meluinen\tGwesgylliel is at Lin Giliath in Meluinen in the North Downs.\n3\tTalk to Gimli in Rivendell\tGimli is currently staying in Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Gwesgylliel has learned that a party of dwarves came to Rivendell not long ago, and one of their company, Gimli, was a champion. This dwarf-champion might be willing to teach you some of his techniques.\n",
[455]="70000034\n1\tComplete Articles of Discovery\030Complete Implements of the Hunt\tFenton Marshley knows of a legendary hunter who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Fenton Marshley\tFenton Marshley is outside the Hunting Lodge east of the town of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land.\n3\tTalk to Legolas in Rivendell\tLegolas may still be in Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Fenton Marshley encountered a party of Elves on his journey through the Mirkwood and believes that one of that company might still have things to teach even a skilled hunter such as yourself.\n",
[456]="700001F5\n1\tComplete Articles of Harmony\030Complete Implements of Song\tBaillindiel knows of a legendary minstrel who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Baillindiel\tBaillindiel is at Celondim, the Elf-harbour in Ered Luin.\n3\tTalk to Lindir\tLindir is in the Hall of Fire in Elrond's home in the vale of Imladris. Baillindiel thinks you should speak with Lindir, for the Elf may be able to provide you with further instruction.\n",
[457]="700001DF\n1\tComplete Articles of Mystery\030Complete Implements of Knowledge\tIsdi knows of a legendary lore-master who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Isdi\tIsdi is at the ruins of Edhelion, on the slopes above Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin.\n3\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is in the library of the Last Homely House, in the Vale of Imladris. The lore-master Isdi believes that Elrond would wish to speak with you, and that you might learn something from his teachings.\n",
[458]="70002E99\n1\tComplete Articles of Fortitude\030Complete Implements of Battle\tWáli knows of a legendary guardian who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Wáli\tThe dwarf Wáli is at the outpost of Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall and west of the dwarf-city of Gondamon in Ered Luin.\n3\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee in Rivendell\tThe whereabouts of Samwise Gamgee are currently unknown to Wáli, but he thinks he might be in Rivendell. Wáli thinks you should speak with Samwise Gamgee, rumoured to be a guardian of unmatched skill, with the hope that he could teach you a thing or two.\n",
[459]="7004450E\n1\tInspect the letter\tLandath was supposed to deliver the letter three days ago. He is so upset he has asked you to examine the letter.\n2\tTalk to Landath\tLandath stands in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Tell Landath that the letter isn't in terrible shape.\n3\tFind Habdir's wax and seal\030Re-seal the letter\tThe Clothiers' Fellow-hall is in the Third Circle, just south of the Pier. Landath feels the letter can still be delivered if the seal is re-made. This can be done with Master Habdir's seal, found in the Clothiers' Fellow-hall.\n4\tReturn to Landath\tLandath stands in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Show Landath that the letter has been re-sealed.\n5\tTalk to Master Aglarang\tMaster Aglarang should be at the Smiths' Fellow-hall, in the northern part of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. The letter should be delivered to a smith named Rhofin. Find Master Aglarang and ask him where Rhofin can be found.\n6\tInquire at the Merry Swan\030Inquire at the Smiths' Market\030Inquire at the Court of Eärnil\tThe Smiths' Market lies just north of the Pier, the Court of Eärnil lies south of the Pier, and the Merry Swan lies on the far south of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. Ask around the Third Circle for the whereabouts of Rhofin the Smith.\n7\tTalk to Landath\tLandath has come along with you on the errand. If you should get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. You have asked after Rhofin in the three locations. See what Landath has to say about it.\n8\tTalk to Rhofin\tThe Forges of Cirion are in the northern stretch of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. Based on the people who had seen Rhofin today, Landath believes he will be working in the Forges of Cirion.\n9\tTalk to Landath\tLandath has come along with you on the errand. If you should get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. See what Landath wishes to do while Rhofin smiths the buckle.\n10\tThe Forges of Cirion are in the northern stretch of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. View some of the other smiths at work while you wait for Rhofin to finish.\t\n11\tTalk to Landath\tLandath has come along with you on the errand. If you should get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. You've watched some of the other smiths at work.\n12\tCheck on Rhofin\tThe Forges of Cirion are in the northern stretch of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. Check on Rhofin to see if he is done with his work.\n13\tTalk to Habdir\tMaster Habdir can be found just south of the Pier in the Third Circle, inside the Clothiers' Fellow-hall. You should deliver the newly-forged buckle to Habdir, Master Clothier, who ordered it.\n14\tTalk to Landath\tLandath has come along with you on the errand. If you should get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call him back. Talk to Landath now that the buckle has been safely delivered.\n15\tMeet Landath back at the Old Guest-house\tThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Meet Landath back at the Old Guest-house.\n",
[460]="70071B7C\n1\tBring Sâdikiz's letter to Mêshaget in Jiret-menêsh\tYou carry a letter given to you by Sâdikiz addressed to Mêshaget. You can't help but notice that the seal on the letter is poorly done and that you would be able to read it without arousing suspicion.\n",
[461]="70042FC0\n1\tBring the letter to Lady Vanyalos in her hall, on the north-east rise in Imloth Melui\tLady Vanyalos can be found in her hall, located on a rise to the north-east of the entrance to Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach. Baranor asked you to deliver a letter describing the attack on Arnach to Lady Vanyalos, who rules Imloth Melui while her husband Forlong is at war.\n",
[462]="7004057B\n1\tTry to rescue Fuirion from Hebil and the Corsairs\tHebil is in the Corsair encampment in northern Lamedon. You should speak with Hebil.\n2\tSpeak with Limril\tGladion and Limril are at their home in Dínadab. You should speak with Limril.\n",
[463]="7006971C\n1\tCollect abandoned research (total: 10)\030Destroy Ghax-hophra nests (total: 8)\tRecover the research and destroy the Ghax-hophra nests.\n2\tDefeat the Ghax-hophra Hive-queen\tDefeat the Ghax-hophra Hive-queen!\n",
[464]="70016026\n1\tTalk to Oxi at Jazârgund\tOxi is at Jazârgund, east of Tharâkh Bazân in Durin's Way. Oxi will be pleased to hear the mirror has been re-aligned and is useful once more.\n",
[465]="70066AE5\n1\tFind Hedra near the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor\tThe location Anoch described sounds like the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor, which lies west of Melgobas. You should try and find Hedra there.\n2\tTalk to Hedra\tYou've found Hedra outside the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor. You should talk to her.\n",
[466]="70023198\n1\tTalk to Dwalin in Frerin's Court\tDwalin is in the courtyard of Frerin's Court in Ered Luin. You should speak with Dwalin if you wish to hear his offer. This is a tutorial quest for accessing the web store.\n",
[467]="7002319C\n1\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook at the Hunter's Lodge\tJon Brackenbrook is at the Hunter's Lodge near Archet. You should speak with Jon Brackenbrook if you wish to learn more about his offer. This is a tutorial quest for accessing the web store.\n",
[468]="70062FA0\n1\tTalk to Skardi Bendblade in his shop.\tSkardi Bendblade is in the blacksmith shop in Mossward. You should speak with Skardi Bendblade to learn more about his offer. This is a tutorial quest for accessing the web store.\n",
[469]="70023199\n1\tTalk to Skardí Bendblade\tTalk to the quest bestower to complete this quest.\n",
[470]="70036FD8\n1\tCollect chicory (total: 8)\tChicory can be found to the south of where Oter and Stithwulf are camped, in the shade of trees. Stithwulf asked you to gather chicory for their supplies.\n2\tPlace the chicory in the crate\tOter's waggon is at his camp to the north of the chicory patches. Oter asked for any chicory you find to be placed in the crate on his waggon.\n3\tTalk to Oter\tOter is at his camp, north of the chicory patches. Oter would like to thank you for helping him bolster their supply of food and medicine before he and Stithwulf leave.\n",
[471]="700261AA\n1\tDeliver the boar-meat to Parr Chopley in Ost Forod\tParr Chopley is in Ost Forod in Evendim, far to the north of the Shire. You should bring the boar-meat to Parr Chopley.\n",
[472]="7002595F\n1\tCollect sand-swept scales (total: 8)\tSand-swept scales can be found on salamanders within the southern dunes of the Barandalf, to the north and east of Dwaling. Wald Hillburrow has asked you to collect sand-swept scales from salamanders, so he can make red glass.\n2\tBring the scales to Wald Hillburrow in Dwaling\tWald Hillburrow is at Hob Hillbrow's just outside of Dwaling. Wald Hillburrow will want to begin grinding down the scales as soon as possible.\n",
[473]="70062DD2\n1\tCollect blades from Uruks near Tham Celechir (total: 8)\tUruks can be found near Tham Celechir, the Hall of the Swift River, to the north of Idhobel.\n2\tBring the Uruk blades to Lornel at Idhobel\tLornel is by the camp-fire at Idhobel.\n",
[474]="7005466A\n1\tCollect venison (total: 5)\030Collect dire-horn meat (total: 5)\tMírthel has asked you to hunt some of the wildlife in Cirith Ungol to assess the edibility of the meat. You should hunt deer and dire-horns for their meat.\n2\tTalk to Mírthel\tMírthel is waiting for you to return with the meat.\n",
[475]="7006AFE0\n1\tAccompany Khôltekh to his study\tAccompany Khôltekh to his study.\n2\tListen to Khôltekh's thoughts on the key\tListen to Khôltekh's thoughts on the key.\n3\tAsk Khôltekh about his thoughts on the matter\tAsk Khôltekh about his thoughts on the matter.\n4\tListen to Khôltekh's explanation\tListen to Khôltekh's explanation.\n5\tListen to Khôltekh's explanation\tListen to Khôltekh's explanation.\n",
[476]="7002C4D7\n1\tAddress your observations of Stangard's hardships to its leaders\tGadda is outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak to Gadda to gain audience with the leaders of Stangard.\n2\tTalk to Gadda\tGadda is outside the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Gadda regarding the council with Stanric.\n",
[477]="7003E6ED\n1\tFind and speak with Orthonn\tOrthonn can be found at his encampment just over the river in Annúndir, not far from the road. You should find and speak with Orthonn.\n",
[478]="7002C000\n1\tTBD\t\n",
[479]="70072F04\n1\tExamine the banner by the long bridge\tStanding by the banner, you know you will be very exposed when you seek to cross the bridge the Ordâkhai constructed. You should be careful.\n2\tLook for threats near the start of the bridge\030Set foot upon the long bridge and begin to cross\tYou should make your way carefully across the bridge. Look for threats when you have begun to cross.\n3\tCompleted\tYou look out for threats near the start of the bridge.\n4\tThink things over when you reach the middle of the bridge\030Make your way to the middle of the bridge\tYou should make your way carefully across the bridge. Think things over when you have reached the middle of the bridge.\n5\tCompleted\tCurious thoughts come to mind as you cross the long bridge.\n6\tListen for danger when you reach the end of the bridge\030Make your way to the end of the bridge\tYou should make your way carefully across the bridge. Listen for danger when you have reached the far end of the bridge.\n7\tCompleted\tYou have crossed the long bridge to Kasukhín without incident.\n",
[480]="70014874\n1\tFind the source of the echo\tThe source of the echo can be found by following the stairs behind Wigfast's hiding place, and heading north-west from there to the upper levels. You should search for the source of the echo.\n2\tInvestigate the rucksack near the rift in the path\tYou spot a rucksack in the north-east corner of the Great Delving, perched near a great rift in the path. You should search the rucksack.\n3\tComplete the first objective in the journal\030Complete the second objective in the journal\tNear the rucksack is a book, a journal, with a dwarf's objectives written down. You should complete the objectives intended by the dwarf who perished.\n4\tTalk to Slagvi in the Dolven-view\tSlagvi is in the Dolven-view in Moria's Great Delving. You should tell Slagvi of all you encountered on the eastern side of the Great Delving.\n",
})
